  "title": "Behistun Inscription",
  "summary": "The Behistun (Bisotun) inscription is a trilingual text in Old Persian, Elamite and Akkadian, set with a relief of Darius I on a cliff in Kermanshah Province, western Iran. It records his victory over rebels including Gaumata and his claim to rule by Ahura Mazda. Rawlinson copied it in 1835, and his work on the Persian portion helped open cuneiform to decipherment.",
